  "details": "When the Creator Companion installs, it's default folder is \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\" Which is reserved for 32-bit applications. This is clearly not a 32-bit application.\n\nWhen selecting \"Install for all users\"\n\nWhen the Creator Companion Uninstalls, it fails to remove the start menu shortcut\n\n \n\nThis really comes off as unprofessional and hacky when you don't do things like this correctly.",
